                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Doctor</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's note: Henry Dewar, doctor. Owned an estate in Lassodie,
                            Fife. Assistant surgeon 30th foot 8.1.1801 fo 1803. MD Edinburgh 1804 De
                            Opthalmia Aegypti. A letter to Thomas Trotter...coal mines (1805). An
                            Inquiry ...Foreign Commerce (read 1.4.1808, dated Lassodie 12.1.1811).
                            Became physician to Manchester Infirmary. Died 8.10.1823, his youngest
                            son Donald William Dewar died at Paris 25.8.1831. </p>
                        <p>We have been unable to trace a pampjhlet Godwin suggests he's reading by
                            Dewar on Malthus, unless this is the piece on foreign commerce.</p>
                        <p>The curiously cramped nature of the dates - around March and Appril 1800,
                            then August September 1803 etc suggests he is visiting London.</p>
                    </note>
